ESSAY · 04 OF 12
:::

:::text id=ZkU-KkIsTM at=center-left width=70% height=216 offsetX=80 offsetY=-176 preset=title align=left color=text
# On the value of slow software
:::

:::text id=oLCQOQ6wUl at=center-left width=70% height=328 offsetX=80 offsetY=120 preset=body align=left color=text
The fastest tool isn't always the best tool. Speed has a cost — it shortens the gap between thinking and shipping, and that gap is where the good ideas live. The best designers I know move quickly only after they've thought slowly. Quick decisions made on top of slow thinking are sharp; quick decisions made on top of more quick decisions just compound the mess.
:::
